<title>NETHERLANDS: Dutch bonds end strong, boosted by soft U.S. CPI.</title>
<headline>Dutch bonds end strong, boosted by soft U.S. CPI.</headline>
<text>
<p>---------------------(Snapshot at 1530 GMT)---------------------</p>
<p>*CASH YIELDS (Dutch state loans)</p>
<p> July 1998 6.25 pct   103.23/31 (+0.04)   bid yield 3.53 (-0.04)</p>
<p> Feb  2002		114.61/71.(+0.45)		 4.78 (-0.10)</p>
<p> Feb  2007 5.75 pct   100.12/20 (+0.87)		 5.73 (-0.12)</p>
<p> Jan  2023		112.96/16 (+1.54)		 6.45 (-0.13)</p>
<p>*FUTURES</p>
<p> BUNDS (June )	 100.80 (+0.89)</p>
<p>TREASURIES (month)  107.63 (+0.94 vs pvs Dutch close)</p>
<p>*DM/NLG		    1.1240 (PREV 1.1242)</p>
<p>--------------------------(SPREADS)----------------------------</p>
<p>*DSLs versus Bunds  (pvs close)    *DSL curve     (pvs close)</p>
<p> 5 yr	  0.00	-0.01	  10-2 yr  220     (228)</p>
<p> 10 yr	-0.09	-0.09	  10-5 yr   95	(97)</p>
<p> Long	 -0.17	-0.16</p>
<p>-------------------------(April 15)-----------------------------</p>
<p>* Dutch bonds end strong, towed up as European markets rejoice over soft U.S. CPI data allaying fears of building price pressures in the economy there for time being. Buoyant mood lures best trade for a week and positive tone may continue for now, brokers say.</p>
